fnmatch on Radix

A cross build cannot run the program that tests fnmatch, so configure
takes it to be there for Linux hosts and for no others. The C library has
fnmatch, as POSIX asks, so PHP's fnmatch() function and the glob stream
wrapper's matching are built for Radix as well.

diff --git a/ext/standard/config.m4 b/ext/standard/config.m4
index 1d64c7ff..686c41b7 100644
--- a/ext/standard/config.m4
+++ b/ext/standard/config.m4
@@ -268,7 +268,7 @@ int main(void) {
 ])
 
 AS_VAR_IF([cross_compiling], [yes],
-  [AS_CASE([$host_alias], [*linux*],
+  [AS_CASE([$host_alias], [*linux*|*radix*],
     [AC_DEFINE([HAVE_FNMATCH], [1])])],
   [AC_FUNC_FNMATCH])
 
